    <bpmn:process id="W_W4739" name="W4739. Third-Party Exit, Transition &amp; Succession Planning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Planned exit (performance, risk, strategic); termination; Critical third party
Frequency: Per exit
Volume: ~30–60 exits/year (planned and unplanned, mostly tail suppliers)
Owner: TPRM Program Manager / Procurement (VS-03)
Participants: Procurement (VS-03), Legal (VS-100.3), IT (VS-27), business owners, alternate vendor (W4737)
Source: workflow W4739 — Third-Party Exit, Transition &amp; Succession Planning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4739_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4739_Lane1" name="TPRM Program Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4739_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4739_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4739_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4739_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4739_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4739_Start3" name="Planned exit (performance, risk, strategic); termination; Critical third party">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4739_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4739_Task4" name="For planned exits (performance/risk/strategic) of material third parties…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: For planned exits (performance/risk/strategic) of material third parties, develop an exit/transition plan: alternate vendor (W4737), data/service migration, transition period, knowledge transfer, and continuity safeguards
Responsible (R): TPRM Program Manager / Procurement / Business / IT
Accountable (A): TPRM Lead / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk / COO
Duration: Per exit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4739_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4739_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4739_Task5" name="Maintain succession/exit readiness for Critical third parties (even when no…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Maintain succession/exit readiness for Critical third parties (even when no exit is planned) so an unplanned termination (breach W4736, financial failure) can be executed within RTO; include contract exit clauses (step-in, transition assistance, data return)
Responsible (R): TPRM Program Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): TPRM Lead / VP Legal
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4739_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4739_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4739_Task6" name="Execute the transition; manage offboarding (W4740); capture lessons and update…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Execute the transition; manage offboarding (W4740); capture lessons and update DD/tiering/contracts (W4741); settle final accounts (VS-15) and contract close-out
Responsible (R): TPRM Program Manager / Procurement / Legal / Finance
Accountable (A): TPRM Lead / COO
Duration: Per exit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4739_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4739_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4739_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4739_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4739_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-715 (ensure controlled execution — Concentration, Resilience, Exit &amp; TPRM Governance/Analytics (PA-161.3).) | - CTL-715: material exits have a transition plan; Critical third parties have exit readiness; contract exit clauses in place
Owner: TPRM Program Manager / Procurement (VS-03)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4739_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4739_Annotation8" targetRef="W4739_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
